# Panels are line-oriented data: keep diffs readable, never CRLF-mangled.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# EXCEPTION, and it must stay LAST -- in .gitattributes the last matching
# pattern wins, so this has to come after the general *.csv rule above.
#
# Figure data CSVs are written by python's csv.writer, which emits CRLF by
# default (RFC 4180). The v10 audit contract is on these files byte-for-byte,
# so git must NOT normalise them: a clone that checked out LF would differ from
# what `make figures` regenerates, and every freeze would show a phantom diff.
figures/*_data.csv -text

# Figures are binary; do not try to diff or merge them.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
